[Variation "Advance Variation, Be3 Blunder"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pawn-grab"]
[Themes "b2-pawn,counting"]
[Kind "against-us"]

1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 Qb6 6. Be3? { Looks natural, guarding d4, but the bishop was the only defender of b2. Black's queen now has a free pawn and a strong attack. }
6... Qxb2! { The queen takes b2 and now attacks the rook on a1 as well. We cannot trap it, and Black is a pawn up with a strong attack. } *
